// The signal graph, as SEGMENTS: each module says where its signal goes next — the lane
// "drums" included, since a lane is a module too. The chains are DERIVED by following the
// arrows — a run breaks where the signal splits, and where two signals meet (which is what
// a bus is).
//
// `bypassed` lists the modules the signal passes through untouched, and on a lane that is
// its mute.

// `MIX` is the mixer's sum and `OUT` is the interface; the run between them is the MASTER
// CHAIN, and `OUT` carries the song's output level as its `Volume`.

// This song has a viewport, so it has the same pair for the PICTURE: `RENDER` is where the
// three video lanes composite and `VIDEO_OUT` is the frame that leaves. Neither carries a
// param — a frame has no level — and neither is written by hand: a project declaring a
// viewport gets the run added when it is opened. See packages/song/docs/videoOutputs.md.

// The video lanes are in this map too, for the same reason the audio ones are: a lane is a
// module. Only "main" is written here — it runs through the shader on its way to the sum — and
// the two that are not named still composite, exactly as an unwired audio lane still plays.
//
// `glow#audio` is the SIDE input: the drums lane feeds the shader's audio port as well as the
// mix, and `uAudio` is that lane's live level. The picture moves with the kit.

// The three shape modules are here too, each wired to the lane that draws it: a shape is a
// picture SOURCE, so it goes INTO a lane the way a camera does. See song-video/docs/shapes.md.
// One lane each, so any of the three can be hidden or run through a shader on its own — and the
// lane is `box_layer` rather than `@workspace/shapes/box` because a lane and a module share one
// name space, and a lane's own name is never namespaced.

modules({
  drums: ["MIX", "@workspace/shaders/glow#audio"],
  MIX: ["OUT"],
  main: ["@workspace/shaders/glow"],
  "@workspace/shaders/glow": ["RENDER"],
  "@workspace/shapes/box": ["box_layer"],
  "@workspace/shapes/dot": ["dot_layer"],
  "@workspace/shapes/title": ["title_layer"],
  RENDER: ["VIDEO_OUT"],
})
